WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:08.179
My name is Brother John, and I am a monk at Croyland Abbey, a monastery on the east coast of England.

2
00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:15.680
This monastery is a religious community of men who live together in seclusion and raise their own food.

3
00:00:15.681 --> 00:00:23.525
Croyland Abbey is self-sustaining, so monks rarely need to leave the monastery, and most never do.

4
00:00:23.526 --> 00:00:33.530
Since this is a Benedictine abbey, we live according to the Rule of St. Benedict, a set of rules created long ago by St. Benedict.

5
00:00:33.531 --> 00:00:40.684
He was an Italian monk who started a monastery about six hundred years ago, just south of Rome.

6
00:00:40.685 --> 00:00:47.485
We spend our days praying, praising God, and working at various jobs in the monastery.

7
00:00:47.486 --> 00:00:56.722
Most of the time, we do not speak. The year is 1150, and I have been here for twenty years.

8
00:00:56.723 --> 00:01:04.435
I am the youngest son of a wheat farmer, and by law, only the oldest son may inherit the family farm.

9
00:01:04.436 --> 00:01:12.721
This law makes it very difficult for younger sons to make a living, so my future was very uncertain.

10
00:01:12.722 --> 00:01:21.464
This worried my father, so when I was seven years old, my father decided to give me to the monks at Croyland Abbey.

11
00:01:21.465 --> 00:01:31.325
My mother cried, and so did I, but my father said the monks would educate me, and I would learn a trade or profession.

12
00:01:31.326 --> 00:01:40.914
He thought I'd have a better chance at a meaningful life, and did not want me to end up as a menial laborer on my brother's farm.

13
00:01:40.915 --> 00:01:45.133
My mother finally agreed to let me go.

14
00:01:45.134 --> 00:01:52.122
For the next five years, I worked in the monastery kitchen and tended the sheep in the pastures.

15
00:01:52.123 --> 00:01:59.939
Every afternoon a monk taught me and the other boys how to read and write using the Holy Scriptures.

16
00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:04.118
We attended chapel, but not as much as the monks.

17
00:02:04.119 --> 00:02:12.619
The monastery cook noticed that I had an interest in herbs because I spent all of my spare time in the garden.

18
00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:23.227
He thought I might make a good herbalist some day, and that made me happy, since I had grown to love the quiet of the monastery gardens.

19
00:02:23.228 --> 00:02:32.843
At the age of 12, I chose to become a novice, which is the first step to becoming a real religious member of a monastery.

20
00:02:32.844 --> 00:02:43.994
During a special ceremony, an older monk shaved a bald patch on the top of my head, which signified that I was a servant of God.

21
00:02:43.995 --> 00:02:55.241
Then I made a vow to follow the Rule of St. Benedict, obey God and the monks, cherish silence, and fulfill all my duties to the monastery.

22
00:02:55.242 --> 00:03:02.782
When I was 15 years old, I took my final vows to become a monk, and I promised never to marry.

23
00:03:02.783 --> 00:03:10.118
I also gave up everything I owned and promised to obey the abbot, the head monk.

24
00:03:10.119 --> 00:03:15.125
There was no turning back, and I would be a monk for life.

25
00:03:15.126 --> 00:03:26.729
Now I work in the herb garden, where I grow many different kinds of plants to make medicine for the other monks or for the village people seeking help.

26
00:03:26.730 --> 00:03:32.214
Another rule of St. Benedict states that the sick should never be forgotten.

27
00:03:32.215 --> 00:03:44.396
Of course monks know that human life is in God's hands, but plants are made by God too, and we believe they should be used to ease human suffering.

28
00:03:44.397 --> 00:03:52.855
To educate myself I spend many hours reading books by the ancient Greeks and by a Persian named Avicenna.

29
00:03:52.856 --> 00:03:58.798
These books have important information about hundreds of plants and the diseases they cure.

30
00:03:58.799 --> 00:04:05.812
They contain instructions on how to grow the plants, and recipes for how to prepare them for certain maladies.

31
00:04:05.813 --> 00:04:10.933
For example, mint is very common in the meadows around the monastery.

32
00:04:10.934 --> 00:04:17.112
When I add mint leaves to boiling water, I can make a tea that cures a stomachache!

33
00:04:17.113 --> 00:04:24.856
Any part of a plant can be used to make medicine, but I usually use the roots, leaves, and seeds.

34
00:04:24.857 --> 00:04:29.330
I collect the plants from the garden and allow them to dry out;

35
00:04:29.331 --> 00:04:37.361
then I crush them into powder so they mix easily with oil, water, honey, or vinegar.

36
00:04:37.362 --> 00:04:45.991
Many times I put the powders I make into small bags and place them on a patient's skin to ease soreness.

37
00:04:45.992 --> 00:04:56.419
A powder made from a yellow flower called feverfew, when mixed with honey, can be taken by mouth to calm a cough and reduce a fever.

38
00:04:56.420 --> 00:05:04.384
If mixed with water and rubbed on the skin, feverfew also stops the itch of an insect bite.

39
00:05:04.385 --> 00:05:08.967
When I became a monk, I was given a plain robe with a hood.

40
00:05:08.968 --> 00:05:15.467
Sometimes I cover my head with the hood when I am in deep thought and do not want to talk to anyone.

41
00:05:15.468 --> 00:05:24.062
Silence is so important to everyone here at Croyland Abbey that monks use hand signals in order not to disturb the stillness.

42
00:05:24.063 --> 00:05:29.563
We have more than one hundred signals that we use at mealtimes alone!

43
00:05:29.564 --> 00:05:38.300
For instance, if I want someone to pass me a plate of fish at dinner, I make a swimming motion with my hands.

44
00:05:38.301 --> 00:05:48.152
One of St. Benedict's rules says that a monk must be ready at all times to serve God, so we sleep in our clothes every night.

45
00:05:48.153 --> 00:05:55.015
Then we awake very early and rush to the chapel to praise God with songs and prayers.

46
00:05:55.016 --> 00:06:02.784
We also have a special prayer book, called a book of hours, which we carry to prayer eight times a day.

47
00:06:02.785 --> 00:06:11.486
When the bell sounds, it means it is time for prayer, and we must stop whatever we are doing and go to the chapel immediately.

48
00:06:11.487 --> 00:06:18.339
We first pray before sunrise, and the final call to prayer is just before bedtime.

49
00:06:18.340 --> 00:06:25.884
Luckily the gardens are not far from the chapel, so it is easy for me to get there without too much trouble.

50
00:06:25.885 --> 00:06:29.106
I love being a monk and a herbalist.

51
00:06:29.107 --> 00:06:36.148
The years of working in the garden and helping my patients have taught me much about the world and God.

52
00:06:36.149 --> 00:06:47.345
It is a quiet, serene life, and I am grateful to my father for putting me on this path so long ago.

